 ### Fixed
+- **`ctx_edit` no longer fails when `old_string` was copied from a compressed
+  `ctx_read` view.** Lossy modes such as `aggressive` (which `auto` can pick)
+  strip blank and comment-only lines, halve space indentation and merge runs of
+  closing braces, so an `old_string` taken from that view never matched the file
+  byte-for-byte and the edit failed. `ctx_edit` now has a last-resort match that
+  compares only significant lines (the same stripping rules, whitespace
+  collapsed). It is applied only when the match is unique and covers whole
+  lines. Unchanged lines are kept verbatim, stripped comments and blank lines
+  inside the span are preserved, and inserted lines are re-indented to the
+  file's style. Ambiguous or content-differing matches still fail as before.
